  "scope": "Small one-warp CTA probes with standard swizzled TK shared tiles. No global transpose, TMA, persistence, or end-to-end performance claim. FP8 W is transposed by native byte LDSM into A. Original BF16 dY is row-loaded and quantized with unchanged row/N32 scales into B. FP32 output is logically transposed via tile indexing; BF16 conversion plus STSM trans produces the original [M,K] output layout.",
  "oracle": "Independent CPU FP64 GEMM on decoded FP8 weight and row/N32-quantized BF16 dY; exact dyadic sums.",
  "assembly_method": "Lexical last-definition audit of each unrolled QMMA weight operand; not a general control-flow analyzer.",
